# Requirements

Parameters a0..a4 are constant levels of inputs c0..c4.

### H1: Zero input leaves the body still

WHEN all constant levels a0..a4 are 0 for the whole trial, THE system SHALL stay near the start pose.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [-0.1, 0.1]
label = "inside"
[prediction.when]
a0 = 0
a1 = 0
a2 = 0
a3 = 0
a4 = 0
```

Result (E1): hit. x=4.8e-5. c0=1 alone: no motion. c1=1 alone: heading +39 deg, x -0.23.

### H2: Inputs c2, c3, c4 each do something to the pose

WHEN only one of a2, a3, a4 is 1 and the rest are 0, THE system SHALL move or turn the body measurably, with at least one of x or heading changing.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "heading"
range = [-180, -5]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
a0 = 0
a1 = 0
a2 = 1
a3 = 0
a4 = 0
```

Result (E2): P1 missed (heading -0.22). Constants on c2,c3,c4 give only a brief transient.

### H3: Oscillating drive on c0 produces sustained displacement

WHEN c0 is a 1 Hz sine of amplitude 1 and the other inputs are 0, THE system SHALL move the body so that x ends above 0.1 m.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.1, 2.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
a0 = 1
a1 = 0
a2 = 0
a3 = 0
a4 = 0
f = 1
```

Result (E3): P1 missed. c0 sine gave x 6.7e-5. c2 sine: x 0.018. c3 sine: heading +30 deg, x 0.006.

### H4: Phase-shifted travelling wave across channels moves the body forward

WHEN all five inputs are 1 Hz sines of amplitude 1 with phase lag ph per channel index, THE system SHALL reach x above 0.2 m with ph = 1.5.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.2, 3.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
a = 1
f = 1
ph = 1.5
```

Result (E4): P1 missed. At 1 Hz, ph 0.5..3.0 gave x -0.097, 0.027, -0.205, 0.007, 0.028, 0.050 and heading 137, -1, -84, -55, -152, -6 deg. The wave rotates the body, non-monotonically in ph. No forward travel.

